# .fork/path-policy -- how an upstream change to a path is handled.
#
#   mirror     take upstream's version (new files, edits, deletions)
#   dropped    the path stays absent: the fork removed it on purpose
#   ours       the fork owns the file: keep ours, report upstream's change
#   protected  upstream must never touch this: a change here stops the sync
#
# Rules are matched in order, first match wins, so exceptions go above the rule
# they except.  The `pruned` line is the built-in rule for the fork's own
# deletions: a path that exists in the accepted upstream revision but not in the
# fork was removed on purpose and stays removed.  Its position matters -- it
# keeps pruned files dropped even when a later `mirror` rule covers their
# directory.
#
# A path that matches nothing is `unknown` and stops the sync: a new upstream
# surface (a new top-level directory, a new installer, ...) is a fork decision,
# not something to absorb silently.

# --- fork control surface -------------------------------------------------
# Upstream has none of this, so a change here means something is wrong.
protected .fork/**
protected .gitmodules
protected third_party/llama.cpp

# --- fork-owned files -----------------------------------------------------
# Upstream edits these heavily (marketing README, installer docs); we keep ours
# and report what changed.
ours .github/**
ours README.md
ours AGENTS.md
ours FORK_NOTES.md
ours .gitignore
ours .gitattributes
ours LICENSE

# --- what we deleted ------------------------------------------------------
pruned

# --- kept data, then everything else under those directories (dropped) ----
mirror data/draft_vocab.bin
mirror data/draft_vocab_en.bin
mirror data/expert-profile.bin
mirror data/expert-profile-coder.bin
dropped data/**

# --- kept benchmarks, then the rest of bench (almost all of it dropped) ---
mirror bench/micro/**
mirror bench/gfx906_qsa_query_swizzle_probe.cpp
mirror bench/test_gfx906_qsa_query_swizzle_guard.py
dropped bench/**

# --- removed platform ports and documentation ----------------------------
dropped docs/**
dropped metal/**
dropped serve/**
dropped sycl/**

# --- the engine: followed from upstream ----------------------------------
mirror CMakeLists.txt
mirror cmake/**
mirror include/**
mirror ref/**
mirror src/**
mirror tests/**
mirror tools/**
